{
	"description": "Golden vectors for the selection case actions (selection_uppercase, selection_lowercase, selection_titlecase and the uppercase_selection / titlecase_selection toggles). Replayed by the macOS, Linux and Windows suites so the three drivers agree on accented letters, apostrophes and hyphens.",
	"title_rule": "Title case lowercases the text, then gives the first character of each word its Unicode title-case form. A word starts at the beginning of the text and after whitespace or a dash (Unicode Pd, e.g. the hyphen of jean-pierre). Other punctuation placed before a word (quotes, brackets, guillemets) is kept and does not consume the capital. An apostrophe inside a word does not start a new word, so l'ete stays L'ete and don't stays Don't. A digit or symbol that starts a word is kept and ends the word start, so 3e stays 3e.",
	"toggle_rule": "toggle_upper returns the uppercase text when the text contains a character with an uppercase mapping, the lowercase text otherwise. toggle_title returns the lowercase text when the text is already in title case, the title-case text otherwise.",
	"drivers_rule": "A vector without a drivers list applies to hs, linux and ahk. The Windows driver uses the operating system's simple case mappings (StrUpper / StrLower), which do not expand ß to SS, do not apply the Greek final sigma and have no title-case digraphs, so those vectors are limited to the two Lua drivers, which read the complete generated Unicode table.",
